WEBVTT

00:10.582 --> 00:11.606
Hello?

00:12.117 --> 00:14.517
Oh, hey, Julia.
I was just on my way over.

00:14.686 --> 00:16.278
Anything I need to bring?

00:16.455 --> 00:19.390
Thai food? Wine? Batteries?

00:21.527 --> 00:23.825
What do you mean, don't come?

00:25.464 --> 00:29.924
Gee, do you really think your psychiatrist
is the best judge of who you sleep with?

00:31.470 --> 00:34.735
Well, sure you could do better.
We could both do better.

00:34.907 --> 00:38.206
But in the meantime,
I am on my way over.

00:38.410 --> 00:40.241
Okay, okay, need to stop you here.

00:40.412 --> 00:44.314
There is a big difference between
"meaningless" and "degrading. "

00:46.385 --> 00:49.786
You know what? I think
we'll just have to agree to disagree.

00:50.456 --> 00:53.584
Okay, then, you have a nice life too.

00:56.395 --> 00:59.387
Why do these women insist
on getting well?

01:00.032 --> 01:02.057
- Hey, Alan...
- Hang on, Charlie.

01:02.234 --> 01:03.826
This is an important moment...

01:04.002 --> 01:05.993
...and I wanna savor it.

01:07.439 --> 01:11.170
Alan J...

01:11.343 --> 01:13.470
...Harper.

01:15.747 --> 01:18.238
What's the big deal?
It's just an alimony check.

01:18.417 --> 01:19.884
Not an alimony check.

01:20.052 --> 01:24.079
This is my final alimony check.

01:26.291 --> 01:27.656
Isn't it beautiful?

01:27.826 --> 01:30.386
Oh, right,
Judith is getting married this weekend.

01:30.562 --> 01:32.462
Exactly.
And you know what that means.

01:32.998 --> 01:34.863
You can finally
kick in a few bucks around here?

01:36.969 --> 01:39.164
Good one. No.

01:39.605 --> 01:41.232
It means Alan gets new underwear.

01:43.775 --> 01:47.074
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I'm going to go pick up my son...

01:47.246 --> 01:51.046
...and deliver this last drop of blood money
to the former Mrs. Alan Harper...

01:51.216 --> 01:54.845
...and soon to be Mrs. Herb Melnick.
May God have mercy on his soul.

01:59.591 --> 02:01.149
Amen.

02:02.628 --> 02:04.960
- So you want some company?
- You wanna come with me?

02:05.130 --> 02:07.121
Yeah, why not? I don't have any plans.

02:07.299 --> 02:09.494
You got stood up again, didn't you?

02:10.736 --> 02:13.728
I'm starting to think all these girls
have the same damn shrink.

02:14.540 --> 02:16.303
If you're gonna come,
grab your camera.

02:16.475 --> 02:19.672
You can take some snapshots
of Pharaoh Judith letting her Alan go.

02:21.013 --> 02:22.605
Got the camera right here.

02:22.781 --> 02:26.273
- You carry it with you?
- Thought I had a date.

02:27.586 --> 02:29.645
Takes video too.

02:57.316 --> 02:58.578
I hand it to you, Charlie.

02:58.750 --> 03:01.378
Stopping at the copy place
was a great idea.

03:01.553 --> 03:04.852
And the picture will make
a terrific Christmas card.

03:06.592 --> 03:09.618
Wanna get the door, Herb?
Stop yelling at me!

03:09.795 --> 03:12.923
I am not yelling. This is yelling!

03:13.098 --> 03:15.464
You know what?
This really isn't that funny.

03:16.702 --> 03:18.795
- Oh, hi, Alan, Charlie.
- Herb.

03:18.971 --> 03:20.438
- Hey.
- Is this a bad time?

03:20.872 --> 03:24.569
The Spanish Inquisition was a bad time.
This is hell.

03:24.743 --> 03:25.869
Come on in.

03:26.345 --> 03:29.644
So, what's going on?
A little pre-wedding jitters?

03:29.815 --> 03:32.875
We could call it that,
but we'd just be sugarcoating hell.

03:33.185 --> 03:36.450
Oh, don't worry. As soon as Judith puts
on that beautiful white gown...

03:36.622 --> 03:39.090
...marches down the aisle...
- She doesn't want white.

03:39.258 --> 03:40.589
Says it makes her look fat.

03:40.959 --> 03:42.824
Oh, well, that's nice.

03:42.995 --> 03:45.657
She wants to look
trim and fit for the honeymoon.

03:45.831 --> 03:48.061
You're sugarcoating hell again, Alan.

03:48.233 --> 03:51.862
You wanna help the guy?
Stop talking and smother him with a pillow.

03:52.070 --> 03:55.836
- Oh, great.
- Hey, there's the blushing bride.

03:56.341 --> 03:58.536
She doesn't look fat at all.

03:59.444 --> 04:01.742
- Go ahead, give her the check.
- What check?

04:02.781 --> 04:06.308
Oh, well,
I figured as long as I was here...

04:06.918 --> 04:11.582
...that I would give you
your last and final alimony check.

04:14.526 --> 04:15.925
Got it.

04:16.528 --> 04:19.088
- What the hell are you doing?
- Just a little souvenir.

04:19.431 --> 04:20.489
I'll go find Jake.

04:21.400 --> 04:23.834
She's being a good sport.
Let's get the big check.

04:24.002 --> 04:26.129
No, forget the big check.
Forget the big check.

04:26.305 --> 04:30.571
So, you know,
I read an interesting story the other day.

04:30.742 --> 04:34.542
Married men live, on average,
10 years longer than single men.

04:34.713 --> 04:36.442
What if they don't want to?

04:36.948 --> 04:39.314
Come on, you and Judith
were meant for each other.

04:39.484 --> 04:42.612
- What could possibly come between you?
- My sister.

04:42.788 --> 04:45.586
- You got a sister?
- Down, Charlie.

04:45.757 --> 04:48.817
She came out to help with the wedding,
but it's not really helping.

04:48.994 --> 04:50.393
- What's she look like?
- Charlie.

04:50.562 --> 04:53.224
- She doesn't have a therapist, does she?
- I swear to God.

04:53.398 --> 04:55.298
So, what do you think?

04:55.467 --> 04:57.958
Should I wear it
or have a vet check it for worms?

04:58.437 --> 05:01.565
No, no, it looks fine.

05:01.740 --> 05:04.675
- Myra, this is Judith's first husband Alan.
- Hi.

05:04.843 --> 05:07.835
So how does this work?
Do you get your original testicles back...

05:08.013 --> 05:09.640
...or does my brother give you his?

05:11.583 --> 05:14.051
Myra, the castration jokes
are getting a little old.

05:14.786 --> 05:15.810
Not at my house.

05:17.189 --> 05:20.716
- This is Alars brother, Charlie.
- Oh, yeah, the booze-riddled sleazebag.

05:21.993 --> 05:23.551
She did not hear that from me.

05:23.729 --> 05:25.993
That's okay.
Not like it's a big secret.

05:26.665 --> 05:29.133
Myra, where the hell is Jake?

05:29.368 --> 05:32.565
- How should I know?
- I asked you to get him ready for his father.

05:32.738 --> 05:37.038
You also asked me
to try on this satin stool sample.

05:37.309 --> 05:39.334
Herb, tell your sister it's a lovely dress.

05:39.511 --> 05:43.971
Herb, tell your fiancée the diet pills
are affecting her judgment, but not her ass.

05:44.282 --> 05:45.943
That's it. She's gotta go.

05:46.118 --> 05:49.952
- I can't throw out family.
- And that's the bitch of it, Herb.

05:52.891 --> 05:56.520
Hey, you know, Charlie and I
were thinking of taking Jake out to a movie.

05:56.695 --> 05:57.889
- We were?
- We were.

05:58.196 --> 06:01.563
- Myra, would you like to join us?
- You didn't say anything about a movie.

06:02.000 --> 06:04.230
I wanted to surprise you.

06:04.403 --> 06:07.861
Hey, you know, that's a great idea.
Go to a movie with Alan and Charlie.

06:08.039 --> 06:10.473
Can I wear my pretty new dress?

06:11.042 --> 06:13.067
Get her out, Herb.

06:13.345 --> 06:16.542
Hey, look what I found in the bushes.

06:27.559 --> 06:30.494
God, I hate family movies.

06:30.662 --> 06:34.826
What, you don't buy the central premise
that a dog can play hockey?

06:36.668 --> 06:39.967
Well, not as a power forward.

06:42.808 --> 06:45.436
Oh, we're flying the friendly skies,
are we?

06:46.845 --> 06:50.042
- After you.
- Why, thank you.

06:52.317 --> 06:55.718
Ahh. So you're staying at Judith's.

06:55.887 --> 06:57.320
Yep.

06:57.489 --> 06:58.922
What did she say about me?

06:59.291 --> 07:03.489
Well, if she's telling the truth, we really
shouldn't be drinking out of the same cup.

07:04.729 --> 07:07.823
That might be the nicest thing
she's ever said about me.

07:08.600 --> 07:11.535
I just don't understand
what my brother sees in her.

07:12.337 --> 07:16.865
You know, 15 years ago,
I asked the exact same question.

07:17.209 --> 07:20.303
Little tip?
Don't do it during the wedding toast.

07:22.314 --> 07:24.475
Maybe you can clear something up
for me.

07:24.649 --> 07:27.209
Herb says
you're a successful jingle writer.

07:27.385 --> 07:29.853
But Judith says you are a drunken,
talentless hack...

07:30.021 --> 07:32.649
...who passed out
and fell into a pit of money.

07:33.758 --> 07:35.282
So, what do you need cleared up?

07:38.396 --> 07:40.921
But, ahem, you have me at a disadvantage.

07:41.099 --> 07:43.067
I don't know why Judith hates you.

07:43.235 --> 07:45.635
Hmm... It's hard to say.

07:45.804 --> 07:49.365
Maybe it's because I'm smart.
Maybe it's because I'm independent.

07:49.541 --> 07:53.477
Maybe it's because I offered my brother
a thousand dollars to call off the wedding.

07:54.579 --> 07:56.547
I did the same thing with my brother.

07:56.882 --> 07:58.372
You did?

07:58.550 --> 08:01.485
Well, actually,
it was a thousand-dollar hooker.

08:04.422 --> 08:06.049
But the thought was the same.

08:11.530 --> 08:13.862
So, Myra...

08:14.065 --> 08:15.157
...what do you do?

08:15.600 --> 08:17.591
I teach high school economics.

08:17.969 --> 08:19.368
Huh.

08:19.571 --> 08:21.766
It may sound like a boring life,
but at night...

08:21.940 --> 08:24.909
...I dress up like a giant spider
and fight crime.

08:26.611 --> 08:30.877
Interesting. Now, did you decide spider
and have the costume made...

08:31.049 --> 08:33.449
...or find the costume and say,
"okay, spider"?

08:35.120 --> 08:37.179
Are you mocking the Scarlet Arachnid?

08:39.190 --> 08:41.124
Sorry, sorry.

08:41.293 --> 08:45.195
It's just hard to believe
that you're Herb's sister. He's so...

08:45.463 --> 08:46.691
Hapless?

08:47.999 --> 08:51.162
I was gonna say tall, but hapless works.

08:51.836 --> 08:54.031
To hapless Herb.

08:55.006 --> 08:56.598
To the Scarlet Arachnid.

08:57.876 --> 08:58.900
Shh.

08:59.077 --> 09:00.601
My enemies are everywhere.

09:03.315 --> 09:05.579
&lt;i>BoTH
Let's all go to the lobby&lt;/i>

09:05.750 --> 09:07.775
&lt;i>Let's all go to the lobby&lt;/i>

09:07.953 --> 09:12.390
&lt;i>Let's all go to the lobby
And have ourselves a treat&lt;/i>

09:14.659 --> 09:16.217
We're here.

09:16.394 --> 09:20.455
- Oh, yes. Judith's house of pain.
- Shh, shh, shh.

09:20.865 --> 09:23.095
Lxnay. That's her idkay.

09:24.002 --> 09:26.368
We're here.

09:27.038 --> 09:29.404
Well, thanks for the movie.

09:30.141 --> 09:33.975
- Wait, wait, wait. I'll walk you.
- Why, thank you.

09:35.013 --> 09:36.002
Whoa-oh!

09:37.349 --> 09:38.441
You okay?

09:38.950 --> 09:41.976
I never know till I sober up.

09:43.455 --> 09:47.084
- I think they like each other.
- Sure, they like each other.

09:47.258 --> 09:49.988
No, I mean they "like" like each other.

09:50.161 --> 09:54.495
Oh, no, Jake. Your Uncle Charlie only
"like" likes a certain type of woman.

09:54.666 --> 09:57.601
- Mom calls them tramps.
- Well...

09:58.536 --> 10:00.697
That's as good a word as any.

10:02.407 --> 10:04.204
Thanks. That was fun.

10:04.376 --> 10:05.934
Yeah, it was.

10:06.111 --> 10:07.271
See you around.

10:07.746 --> 10:09.213
Yeah.

10:12.150 --> 10:14.175
I'm sorry. I don't know why I did that.

10:14.953 --> 10:16.113
Who cares?

10:18.390 --> 10:21.223
Looks like Aunt Myra's a tramp, huh?

10:28.800 --> 10:31.166
Oh, come on, Judith,
so he gave her a kiss.

10:31.336 --> 10:32.496
It's no big deal.

10:32.671 --> 10:34.901
Yeah, that's how Charlie says goodbye.

10:35.073 --> 10:37.371
Yep, some people shake hands,
some people wave.

10:37.542 --> 10:40.340
My brother darts his tongue
in and out of your mouth.

10:41.112 --> 10:43.637
- What did I miss?
- You know Dr. Melnick?

10:43.815 --> 10:45.305
The guy your mom's marrying?

10:45.483 --> 10:48.008
- He has a sister...
- Got it.

10:49.154 --> 10:51.679
I'm sure it has nothing to do
with you, Judith.

10:51.856 --> 10:53.153
Wait, hang on a second.

10:53.425 --> 10:55.359
- Are you done with your breakfast?
- Yeah.

10:55.527 --> 10:57.188
- Then get out.
- Fine.

10:57.362 --> 10:59.728
- Berta will just tell me later, right?
- Right.

11:03.601 --> 11:04.898
Okay, Judith, that's insane.

11:05.070 --> 11:07.732
Charlie would not do
Myra just to piss you off.

11:07.906 --> 11:09.533
I don't think.

11:09.974 --> 11:11.771
How would I know what he sees in her?

11:11.943 --> 11:13.774
She got working girl-parts?

11:15.780 --> 11:18.408
You know what, you leave.
Send Jake back.

11:20.185 --> 11:23.313
Okay, okay, fine, fine, I'll talk to him.

11:23.822 --> 11:24.846
I don't know.

11:25.457 --> 11:27.425
I'll tell him to keep his hands off Myra.

11:27.592 --> 11:29.651
And then I'll tell the rain not to fall...

11:29.828 --> 11:32.558
...the Earth not to spin,
and you to stop nagging me.

11:39.938 --> 11:42.372
Oh, boy, I'm gonna pay for that.

11:43.007 --> 11:45.737
&lt;i>You know what your problem is?
Phone cojones.&lt;/i>

11:46.211 --> 11:48.475
- Excuse me?
- When you're on the phone with her...

11:48.646 --> 11:50.409
...you got boulders between your legs.

11:52.117 --> 11:55.484
The minute you hang up
you're as smooth as a Ken doll.

11:56.788 --> 11:59.052
&lt;i>Phone cojones.&lt;/i>

11:59.324 --> 12:01.155
Good to have a name for it.

12:01.326 --> 12:03.055
So tell me about the sister.

12:03.394 --> 12:05.487
I don't know.
She doesn't seem like his type.

12:05.663 --> 12:08.291
What, no coin slot in her forehead?

12:09.033 --> 12:10.557
- Morning.
Morning.

12:10.735 --> 12:12.828
Charlie, we need to talk about Myra.

12:13.004 --> 12:15.768
- Yeah, that was probably a mistake.
- It was?

12:16.107 --> 12:19.076
She's a nice kid,
but she's just not, you know...

12:19.377 --> 12:22.073
A red-hot simpleton with no self-respect?

12:24.616 --> 12:26.982
I hope she didn't take
that kiss thing too seriously.

12:27.152 --> 12:30.781
- So you're not planning on pursuing her?
- No, no, no.

12:30.955 --> 12:33.583
In fact, I got a date tonight
with a lovely sex addict...

12:33.758 --> 12:35.419
...whose therapist is on vacation.

12:36.861 --> 12:40.524
It's what we eligible bachelors call
"a window of opportunity. "

12:42.167 --> 12:45.659
You know, there's a special section
in hell reserved for people like you.

12:47.038 --> 12:50.303
That's good because I'd hate
to have to stand on line.

12:51.543 --> 12:55.001
So I'm like, "Yeah, I can make
a lot of money as a lingerie model...

12:55.180 --> 12:57.978
...but then who's gonna take me
seriously as a director?"

12:58.983 --> 13:02.214
- Good point.
- Sometimes I wish I wasrt beautiful.

13:02.387 --> 13:04.548
I mean, ugly people have it
so easy, you know?

13:05.356 --> 13:07.847
- I've heard.
- So, what about you?

13:08.026 --> 13:10.893
- Still writing jingles?
- Just during the day.

13:11.062 --> 13:14.122
At night I dress up as a big spider
and fight crime.

13:14.299 --> 13:16.460
Huh. You know, I dated a cop once.

13:16.634 --> 13:20.593
Well, it wasrt so much a date
as a way to get out of a ticket. Heh.

13:20.772 --> 13:21.966
Interesting.

13:22.407 --> 13:26.707
- Okay, here we are.
- Oh, I hope this place has fresh lobster.

13:26.878 --> 13:29.472
That frozen stuff is just disgusting.

13:45.964 --> 13:48.398
You know what, Herb?
Forget it, I'll do it myself.

13:48.566 --> 13:50.124
I said I would do it, I'll do it.

13:50.301 --> 13:52.496
Ugh. For God's sake, Judith,
get off his back.

13:52.670 --> 13:55.935
No one's talking to you, Myra.
Okay, everyone calm down.

13:56.107 --> 13:57.369
I'm doing it.

13:58.710 --> 14:01.008
- Oh, hi, Charlie.
- Hi, Herb.

14:01.179 --> 14:03.739
Just taking out the trash.

14:04.349 --> 14:07.443
Yeah, I'm coming
from doing the same thing.

14:08.486 --> 14:10.283
Great, he leaves the door wide o...

14:10.455 --> 14:12.013
What the hell are you doing here?

14:12.490 --> 14:13.650
That's a good question.

14:13.825 --> 14:15.918
- See, the thing is, I...
- oh, hey, Charlie.

14:16.628 --> 14:18.118
Hi, Myra.

14:18.296 --> 14:21.094
No, no. I forbid it. Not in my house.

14:21.633 --> 14:24.693
What brings you to the cul-de-sac
of the damned?

14:25.403 --> 14:26.700
Just in the neighborhood.

14:27.171 --> 14:28.900
That's nice. Come on in.

14:29.774 --> 14:31.298
Thanks.

14:32.243 --> 14:34.711
I said no. Doesrt anybody listen to me?

14:34.879 --> 14:36.403
I'm doing it, look!

14:40.184 --> 14:43.620
You know, I really didn't expect
to see you again.

14:43.788 --> 14:46.916
- Well, I wasrt doing anything, so...
No, Alan, listen to me.

14:47.258 --> 14:49.283
He's here right now.

14:49.861 --> 14:51.385
Why would I kid about that?

14:51.829 --> 14:54.161
I don't know,
maybe his other date didn't work out.

14:58.569 --> 15:00.969
Ah. The plot thickens.

15:01.406 --> 15:03.271
Okay, okay, I can explain.

15:05.076 --> 15:06.703
No, I can't.

15:07.478 --> 15:08.775
Give it a shot.

15:10.048 --> 15:11.379
Well...

15:11.549 --> 15:15.679
...I was with this girl and I suddenly realized
that I'd rather be with someone...

15:15.853 --> 15:19.254
...who I, you know,
actually enjoy being with.

15:19.691 --> 15:21.625
Oh, just forget it, Alan. You're useless.

15:22.126 --> 15:24.094
Herb, do something.

15:24.662 --> 15:26.425
Hey.

15:27.765 --> 15:30.461
I'm going out for ice cream.
Anyone wanna join me?

15:30.802 --> 15:34.829
Charlie, whers the last time
you had a cone with sprinkles?

15:35.540 --> 15:38.998
You know what, Herb? Judith can relax.
I'm gonna check into a hotel.

15:39.177 --> 15:41.509
Myra, no. You don't have to do that.

15:41.679 --> 15:43.271
Yes, she does.

15:43.448 --> 15:46.281
Hey, she's my sister,
she can stay as long as she wants.

15:47.151 --> 15:49.051
I really appreciate this.

15:49.220 --> 15:51.552
- I'll go get my stuff.
- Hey, wait, wait, wait.

15:51.723 --> 15:54.385
You don't have to stay at a hotel.
I got room at my place.

15:54.559 --> 15:57.153
- Yeah, I'll bet you do.
- No, no, no.

15:57.328 --> 15:58.795
No strings attached.

15:59.364 --> 16:00.797
- Really?
- Really.

16:03.067 --> 16:05.797
- Still, I couldn't impose like that.
- It's no imposition.

16:05.970 --> 16:08.063
It's a big house.
There's plenty of room.

16:08.406 --> 16:10.738
- You're sure?
- Absolutely.

16:11.342 --> 16:14.106
Okay, then, I'll be right back.

16:14.278 --> 16:15.745
Herb!

16:17.181 --> 16:18.341
You wanna come too?

16:21.919 --> 16:23.011
Are you nuts?

16:23.187 --> 16:25.655
With Myra out of the house,
I might get lucky tonight.

16:27.058 --> 16:29.049
Really? She seems pretty angry.

16:29.527 --> 16:31.085
It's better when she's angry.

16:33.064 --> 16:35.191
Coming, pookie.

16:43.207 --> 16:45.505
This just sucks.

16:45.676 --> 16:47.644
It's for a couple of days
till the wedding.

16:47.812 --> 16:50.110
Yeah, but why does she have to stay
in my room?

16:50.281 --> 16:53.580
Because... I don't know, you're the kid.

16:53.885 --> 16:55.512
Yeah, well, it's not fair.

16:55.820 --> 16:57.253
Yeah, well, get over it.

17:00.958 --> 17:02.687
Oh, my God!

17:02.860 --> 17:04.259
Jake, that's disgusting.

17:04.429 --> 17:06.192
Yeah, well, get over it.

17:08.966 --> 17:10.934
Go to sleep.

17:14.906 --> 17:16.464
Did you brush your teeth?

17:16.641 --> 17:18.541
Dad, I'm asleep.

17:19.043 --> 17:20.442
Go brush your teeth.

17:20.611 --> 17:24.012
- I can't. I don't have my toothbrush.
- Well, go get it.

17:24.182 --> 17:28.312
